  "question": {
    "text": "To measure the internal resistance of a battery, potentiometer is used. For $\\mathrm{R}=10 \\Omega$, the balance point is observed at $l=500 \\mathrm{~cm}$ and for $\\mathrm{R}=1 \\Omega$ the balance point is observed at $l=400 \\mathrm{~cm}$. The internal resistance of the battery is approximately :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$0.2 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$0.3 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$0.4 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$0.1 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let potential gradient be $\\lambda$.\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{i} \\times 10=\\lambda \\times 500=\\varepsilon-\\mathrm{ir}_{\\mathrm{s}} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 500 \\lambda=\\varepsilon-50 \\lambda \\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{s}}\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Also,\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{i}^{\\prime} \\times 1=\\lambda \\times 400=\\varepsilon-\\mathrm{i}^{\\prime} \\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{s}} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 400 \\lambda=\\varepsilon-400 \\lambda \\mathrm{r}_5 \\\\\n& \\therefore 100 \\lambda=350 \\lambda \\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{s}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{s}}=\\frac{10}{35} \\approx 0.3 \\Omega\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}